      "comments": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228041",
      "image": null,
      "content": "Running untrusted code from LLM agents inside full containers is often too slow and heavy, while raw host execution is a security disaster. Anthropic has open-sourced sandbox-runtime, the exact engine powering local isolation in Claude Code.\n\nInstead of requiring Docker or virtual machines, this package hooks into operating system primitives directly. On macOS, it compiles dynamic Seatbelt profiles via sandbox-exec. On Linux, it provisions network namespaces and filesystem mounts with bubblewrap. On Windows, it binds Windows Filtering Platform egress filters with write-restricted tokens and explicit NTFS access lists.\n\nWhat makes this especially compelling for agent builders is the built-in MCP integration. You can wrap standard Model Context Protocol servers under strict allow-only network domains, Unix socket whitelists, and masked environment variables simply by swapping the execution command. It even handles automated AWS SigV4 request signing with credentials stripped out of process memory.\n\nIf you are designing agent runtimes that must execute shell commands or file operations safely on user machines, this library offers a battle-tested blueprint."
